**Evidence summary:**
- Routing: ✅ `host_1_1_1_1 → switch_dist_1_1 → router_core_1 → router_core_3 → switch_server_access → 10.200.0.3` — full end-to-end ICMP and HTTP work
- DNS: ❌ Every query returns `REFUSED` with `"recursion requested but not available"` — `named.conf` on `dns_server` has `recursion no;` explicitly set
- `host_1_1_1_1` has `nameserver 10.200.0.2` in `/etc/resolv.conf` — it relies entirely on this server for name resolution
- Only queries authoritative to the `local` zone (`web0.local`, etc.) resolve; everything else is refused

